        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Carsten Erik Olsen, S. P. L. Sørensen\n- Organizations: Carlsberg Laboratory\n- Roles: plant ecologist, plant physiologist, chemist\n- Concepts: plant nutrition, soil pH, pH scale, acidity, alkalinity\n\nFacts:\n- S. P. L. Sørensen was a Danish chemist who introduced the concept of pH as a scale for measuring acidity and alkalinity.\n- Carsten Erik Olsen was a Danish plant ecologist and plant physiologist who pioneered the study of plant nutrition in soils of different pH.\n- Carsten Erik Olsen was employed by the Carlsberg Laboratory as an assistant to S. P. L. Sørensen and later worked in his own laboratory.",
